# Line endings are LF everywhere in this repo.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout using the Git-for-Windows default
# (core.autocrlf=true, set in the system gitconfig) rewrites every text file to
# CRLF in the working tree even though the stored blobs are LF-only. `npm run
# lint` (biome check, formatter.lineEnding defaults to "lf") then reports a
# formatting violation on every file it covers, and the lefthook pre-commit
# biome hook fails the same way -- on files that are byte-identical to HEAD.
# CI, Linux and macOS never see it, so it reads as a phantom local failure.
#
# Declaring the attributes here makes git normalize on checkout regardless of a
# contributor's local autocrlf setting. No stored blob changes: as of this
# commit no text blob in history contains a CR byte.
#
# One-time fix for a working tree that is already CRLF. Do NOT reach for
# `git add --renormalize .`. Measured on this repo, it stages nothing (a CRLF
# working file cleans to the identical LF blob), leaves every file CRLF, and
# only refreshes the stat cache -- which silences the 891 "modified" entries
# git status reports for those files. That hides the symptom while lint stays
# red. The files have to be rewritten, so remove and restore them:
#
#     git ls-files -z | xargs -0 rm -f && git checkout -- .
#
# (a fresh clone does the same). Commit real work first -- that command discards
# uncommitted changes to tracked files.

# Default: let git classify text vs binary, and check text out as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Source and config, pinned explicitly so a heuristic miss can't opt a file out.
*.ts     text eol=lf
*.tsx    text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.cjs    text eol=lf
*.mjs    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.jsonc  text eol=lf
*.css    text eol=lf
*.html   text eol=lf
*.svg    text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.toml   text eol=lf
*.lock   text eol=lf
*.rs     text eol=lf
*.nsh    text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Binary. Every image tracked here carries stray CR bytes inside its pixel data,
# so leaving them to the text heuristic is a corruption risk worth not taking.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary

# Tauri updater signing key: byte-exact, never converted in either direction.
.tauri/updater.key.pub -text

# cmd.exe can mis-parse an LF-only batch file, so these stay CRLF on checkout.
*.bat    text eol=crlf
*.cmd    text eol=crlf
